<div class="ca-inner"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Your financial co-pilot</p><h2>Finance leadership that connects<br/>the numbers to the next decision.</h2><p class="ca-intro">Centripetal provides embedded fractional CFO support for early-stage SaaS companies. We bring financial strategy and operating discipline together: the cash model, the capital plan, the board conversation, and the finance work that supports them.</p><div class="ca-split"><div><h3>Built for Seed through Series A</h3><p>Our focus is SaaS founders whose financial complexity has outgrown founder-owned spreadsheets and periodic bookkeeping. Companies with $2M+ in recurring revenue and/or $5M–$15M raised are a useful starting point for a conversation. The fit depends on your decisions, team, and operating needs.</p></div><div><h3>One connected finance function</h3><p>These areas of support work together within an agreed engagement. A fundraise draws on the same customer schedules, financial model, and reporting cadence your team needs to operate after the round.</p><a class="ca-link" href="guides/saas-finance-scorecard.html">Start with your finance foundation →</a></div></div><div class="ca-service-scope"><h2>One engagement.<br/>Connected responsibilities.</h2><p class="ca-intro">These service areas connect within an embedded finance role. The work can extend from financial strategy to the accounting foundation, capital processes, revenue and sales analysis, tax and tax-credit coordination, and back-office ownership. We agree the responsibilities with your team and the specialists involved.</p><div class="ca-split"><div><h3>Begin with the work that needs an owner.</h3><p>An approaching financing, a revised hiring plan, a sharper board question, or an unreliable close can be the starting point. We review the existing records and processes, then prioritize the dependencies behind that decision.</p></div><div><h3>Make the outputs usable.</h3><p>A maintained model, a rolling cash forecast, financial schedules, succinct board materials, and a clear responsibility map should work together. The scope and cadence follow the company’s needs; these are examples rather than a fixed package or timetable.</p><a class="ca-link" href="about.html">Meet the firm behind the work →</a></div></div></div><h2 style="margin-top:64px">The work we help you own.</h2><div class="ca-grid"><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Financial leadership</p><h3>Fractional CFO for SaaS</h3><p class="ca-service-trigger">Finance still runs through the founder.</p><p>Connect the operating model, finance owners, capital decisions, and reporting cadence.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/fractional-cfo-for-saas.html">Explore Fractional CFO for SaaS →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Capital strategy</p><h3>Fundraising Readiness</h3><p class="ca-service-trigger">A raise is approaching.</p><p>Prepare financial statements, customer schedules, cap table records, and use-of-proceeds scenarios.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/fundraising-readiness.html">Explore Fundraising Readiness →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Cash visibility</p><h3>Cash Flow &amp; Runway Planning</h3><p class="ca-service-trigger">Cash timing could change a commitment.</p><p>Maintain a rolling 13-week cash view and compare hiring, collections, and financing scenarios.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/cash-flow-runway-planning.html">Explore Cash Flow &amp; Runway Planning →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Investor communication</p><h3>Board &amp; Investor Reporting</h3><p class="ca-service-trigger">The board needs a clearer decision.</p><p>Explain budget variances, operating assumptions, customer concentration, and the cash outlook.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/board-investor-reporting.html">Explore Board &amp; Investor Reporting →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Financing decisions</p><h3>Venture Debt Readiness</h3><p class="ca-service-trigger">A debt facility is under consideration.</p><p>Connect lender evidence, proposed terms, draw timing, and repayment to the full capital plan.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/venture-debt-readiness.html">Explore Venture Debt Readiness →</a></article><article class="ca-card"><p class="ca-eyebrow">Operating foundation</p><h3>Treasury &amp; Finance Operations</h3><p class="ca-service-trigger">Approvals or handoffs are becoming fragile.</p><p>Clarify banking controls, the QuickBooks or Xero foundation, close ownership, and specialist coordination.</p><a class="ca-link" href="services/treasury-finance-operations.html">Explore Treasury &amp; Finance Operations →</a></article></div><div class="ca-split" style="margin-top:64px"><div><h3>How the engagement begins</h3><ol><li><strong>Map the decision and deadline.</strong> Identify the financing, cash, board, or operational question and the people who own it today.</li><li><strong>Review the supporting foundation.</strong> Examine the books, customer schedules, cap table, model, cash view, and handoffs relevant to that question.</li><li><strong>Agree the work and cadence.</strong> Name priorities, deliverables, owners, and specialist responsibilities; revisit them as the company changes.</li></ol></div><div><h3>What you should expect to use</h3><p>A maintained operating model, cash visibility, clear reporting, and a finance lead who can explain the assumptions. The exact deliverables follow your needs and the agreed scope.</p><a class="ca-link" href="guides/series-a-diligence-readiness.html">See the evidence investors ask for →</a></div></div><h2 style="margin-top:56px">Questions founders ask.</h2><details><summary>How does a fractional CFO work with our bookkeeper?</summary><p>Your bookkeeper records and reconciles transactions. Centripetal connects the books to forecasts, financing decisions, reporting, and finance operations, coordinating with your existing team and specialists.</p></details><details><summary>Is this only support for a fundraise?</summary><p>Fundraising is one inflection point. The same financial foundation supports ongoing hiring, spending, board reporting, treasury, and operating decisions. Engagement priorities can evolve with the company.</p></details><details><summary>What happens when we need an internal finance leader?</summary><p>The finance infrastructure should support that transition. Centripetal can help with the move to an internal VP Finance or finance leader, with documented processes and a clear handoff.</p></details><details><summary>What should we bring to the first conversation?</summary><p>Start with the decision or deadline, who owns finance today, and where your current model, reporting, or processes are falling short. You do not need to upload financial documents to begin the conversation.</p></details><details><summary>Are these six separate packages?</summary><p>They describe connected areas of finance work. The engagement scope follows the company’s needs, including coordination with its existing team and specialists.</p></details><p class="ca-footer"><a class="ca-link" href="contact.html?topic=finance-leadership&amp;from=services-overview#conversation-form">Discuss the finance work that needs an owner →</a></p></div>
